    "intro_narrative": "The year is 2142, and the neon-drenched metropolis above has long forgotten the subterranean servers of Chronos Corp. You are a rogue netrunner who made a critical mistake during a routine data heist, resulting in your consciousness being trapped inside this decaying digital labyrinth. The air around you, though simulated, smells heavily of ozone and burning synthetic coolant. The facility's automated defense systems are slowly waking up from their decades-long hibernation, and their hostile sweepers are already hunting your presence. Your only way out is to initiate the facility's master override sequence to force a hard reboot of the exit ports. To do this, you must navigate a tangled web of obsolete corporate hardware, decrypting secure signals, and rerouting power through various legacy nodes. The architecture here is relentless and unforgiving. If you don't manage to execute the master override in time, your consciousness will be permanently wiped from the net, leaving you as nothing more than ghost code. Find the correct sequence of inputs, carefully follow the data trails, and activate the final execution sequence before the system purges you forever.",
    "narrative_style": "cyberpunk"
  },
